L000478	A summary of standard parameters is given in Table \ref{tab:beam_params}. Each cycle involved the injection of vertically (vector-) polarized deuterons into the COSY ring, bunching and accelerating the beam to \qty{970}{\MeV\per c}, electron cooling to reduce emittance
L000479	and orbit corrections. After starting the extraction onto a carbon target for polarization measurements the deuteron spins were rotated into the horizontal plane using an rf solenoid. The spin precession was continuously monitored, and the rf frequency and phase of the Wien filter was adjusted accordingly to keep a constant phase between the Wien filter rf and the spin precession phase (phase locking)~\cite{Eversmann:2015jnk,PhysRevAccelBeams.28.062801}.
